### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Colección REST — flujos del módulo SUBMISSIONS (Entrega 2)
### Responsable: Ruiz Akle, Juan.
### Cubre: cargar resultado esperado, enviar query, polling, filtros.
### Compatible con VS Code REST Client e importable a Postman.
###
### Cómo usar:
###   1) docker compose up -d
###   2) Ejecutar ruiz-flows.http hasta dejar un reto publicado con
###      esquema + dataset (sección 3 de ese archivo).
###   3) Hacer login en este archivo (sección 1) y rellenar tokens.
###   4) Cargar el resultado esperado (sección 2).
###   5) Probar los flujos de envío y polling (secciones 3-6).
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

@host = http://localhost:3000/api

@adminToken = REEMPLAZAR_ADMIN_TOKEN
@profToken  = REEMPLAZAR_PROFESSOR_TOKEN
@studToken  = REEMPLAZAR_STUDENT_TOKEN

@profId       = REEMPLAZAR_PROFESSOR_ID
@studId       = REEMPLAZAR_STUDENT_ID
@challengeId  = REEMPLAZAR_CHALLENGE_ID
@submissionId = REEMPLAZAR_SUBMISSION_ID

### =======================================================================
### 1. AUTH — login
### =======================================================================

### 1.1 Login PROFESSOR (mismo seed de ruiz-flows.http)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "prof.demo@sqljudge.local",
  "password": "Profe123!"
}

### 1.2 Login STUDENT
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "stud.demo@sqljudge.local",
  "password": "Stud123!"
}

### =======================================================================
### 2. EXPECTED RESULT — el profesor carga el resultado de referencia
###    (requisito para que el reto pueda recibir envíos)
### =======================================================================

### 2.1 Upsert: clientes con > 3 compras (ejemplo del reto del demo)
PUT {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/expected-result
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "columns": ["name", "total"],
  "rows": [
    ["Ana",   8],
    ["Beto",  6],
    ["Carla", 4]
  ],
  "orderSensitive": false,
  "floatTolerance": 0
}

### 2.2 GET — consultar lo que quedó cargado
GET {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/expected-result
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}

### 2.3 ERROR — fila con cardinalidad incorrecta → 400
PUT {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/expected-result
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "columns": ["name", "total"],
  "rows": [["Ana", 8, "extra"]]
}

### 2.4 ERROR — columnas duplicadas (case-insensitive) → 400
PUT {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/expected-result
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "columns": ["Name", "name"],
  "rows": [["Ana", "Beto"]]
}

### =======================================================================
### 3. SUBMISSION — el estudiante envía su query (variante REST-ish)
### =======================================================================

### 3.1 Envío feliz — el stub del worker devuelve exactamente lo esperado
###     y el comparador lo marca ACCEPTED.
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "SELECT c.name, COUNT(o.id) AS total FROM customers c JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id GROUP BY c.name HAVING COUNT(o.id) > 3"
}

### 3.2 Envío forzado a WRONG_ANSWER (marcador en comentario, soportado por el stub)
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "SELECT c.name, COUNT(o.id) AS total /* expect:WRONG */ FROM customers c JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id GROUP BY c.name"
}

### 3.3 Envío forzado a TIME_LIMIT_EXCEEDED
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "SELECT 1 /* expect:TIMEOUT */"
}

### 3.4 Envío forzado a SYNTAX_ERROR
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "SELECT 1 /* expect:SYNTAX */"
}

### 3.5 Envío forzado a RUNTIME_ERROR
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "SELECT 1 /* expect:RUNTIME */"
}

### =======================================================================
### 4. SUBMISSION — variante legacy con challengeId en el body
### =======================================================================

### 4.1 POST /submissions (compatibilidad con clientes existentes)
POST {{host}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "query": "SELECT c.name, COUNT(o.id) AS total FROM customers c JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id GROUP BY c.name HAVING COUNT(o.id) > 3"
}

### =======================================================================
### 5. POLLING / DETALLE / LISTADOS
### =======================================================================

### 5.1 Polling: el estudiante consulta el resultado de su submission
GET {{host}}/submissions/{{submissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}

### 5.2 Detalle (PROFESSOR — dueño del reto)
GET {{host}}/submissions/{{submissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}

### 5.3 Mis submissions (STUDENT, hasta 50 más recientes)
GET {{host}}/submissions/my
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}

### 5.4 Listar con filtros (STUDENT) — ignora studentId distinto del propio
GET {{host}}/submissions?challengeId={{challengeId}}&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}

### 5.5 Listar con filtros (PROFESSOR) — solo retos suyos
GET {{host}}/submissions?challengeId={{challengeId}}&studentId={{studId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}

### 5.6 Atajo PROFESSOR — submissions de un reto ordenadas por score
GET {{host}}/submissions/challenge/{{challengeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}

### =======================================================================
### 6. CASOS BORDE / VALIDACIONES (deben fallar con 400/403/404)
### =======================================================================

### 6.1 Query no SELECT → 400
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "DELETE FROM customers WHERE id > 0" }

### 6.2 Query con DDL escondido → 400
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "SELECT * FROM customers; DROP TABLE orders;" }

### 6.3 STUDENT pide submission ajena → 404 (no leakea existencia)
GET {{host}}/submissions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}

### 6.4 STUDENT pasa studentId de otro usuario → se ignora silenciosamente
GET {{host}}/submissions?studentId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{studToken}}

### 6.5 PROFESSOR intenta cargar expected en reto ajeno → 403
PUT {{host}}/challenges/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/expected-result
Authorization: Bearer {{profToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "columns": ["x"], "rows": [[1]] }

### 6.6 STUDENT no inscrito intenta enviar → 404 (no leakea el reto)
###     (requiere un STUDENT de otro curso para verificarlo en demo)
POST {{host}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer REEMPLAZAR_OTRO_STUDENT_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "SELECT 1 /* sanity */ FROM customers" }
